    <div class="content-asset customer-service-section-8"><!-- dwMarker="content" dwContentID="f5ecc285d51411a1da5bcf3c71" -->
        <div class="customer-service-section-8 text-white pt-3 text-center bg-color-blue" id="cookinginstructions">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row row-cols-1">
      <div class="col-lg-3">
        <img src="/images/content/customer-service-section-8-content-m-cropped.png"
          alt="Cooking Instructions">
      </div>
      <div class="col-lg-9">
        <h2 class="mt-4 mb-4">Defrosting and Cooking Instructions</h2>
        <p>See our <a href="/en-US/chicken-defrosting-guide.html" class="text-decoration-none">
            <span class="color-yellow font-italic">
              Chicken Defrosting Guide
            </span>
          </a> and <a href="/en-US/beef-defrosting-guide.html" class="text-decoration-none">
            <span class="color-yellow font-italic">
              Beef Defrosting Guide
            </span>
          </a> for tips and tricks that will help you safely and effectively thaw products.</p>
        <p>Cook all food to these minimum internal temperatures as measured with a food thermometer before removing food
          from the heat source.</p>
        <div class="text-left max-auto">
          <ul>
            <li>Beef, pork, veal and lamb (steaks, chops and roasts) should be cooked to 145 F and allowed to rest for
              at
              least 3 minutes.</li>
            <li>Ground meats should be cooked to 160 F. </li>
            <li>All poultry (breasts, whole bird, legs, thighs,
              wings, ground poultry, giblets and stuffing) should be cooked to 165 F. </li>
          </ul>
          <a class="btn btn-link-unstyled"
            href="https://www.fsis.usda.gov/wps/portal/fsis/topics/food-safety-education/get-answers/food-safety-fact-sheets/safe-food-handling/safe-minimum-internal-temperature-chart/ct_index usda.gov"
            target="_blank" title="usda.gov">
            <p class="color-white">
              Source: usda.gov
            </p>
          </a>
        </div>
        <p>For more cooking inspiration, check out our <a href="/en-US/cooking-ideas.html"
            class="text-decoration-none">
            <span class="color-yellow font-italic">
              Cooking Guides
            </span>
          </a> and <a href="/en-US/recipes/" class="text-decoration-none">
            <span class="color-yellow font-italic">
              Recipe Finder
            </span>
          </a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
